            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_10",
            "review_title": "Review at Cowboy Jack's Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Mike D\nHua Hin, Thailand671 contributions\n0\nDo not order the ribs!\nMay 2018 • Couples\nI had spotted this place the previous day while checking out Saigon Center, it looked good so we decided to return.\n\nWe took a seat and menus were brought over. I ordered the Mini Burger platter which included Beef, Pork, and Chicken burgers, a small salad and some vegetable chips. My girlfriend ordered American BBQ Ribs which came with Fries and Cornbread.\n\nOur orders arrived and we both started eating. I liked all three of the burgers and would rate them a 4. There were three ribs on my girlfriends plate, the first one was good but I could see her struggling with the second one, it was too tough to chew so she tried to cut the meat with a knife. Now we all know that a properly prepared BBQ rib does not require a fork or knife, the meat should just fall off the bone. After giving up on rib number two she tried rib number three, no luck, you would need a chainsaw and jaws of steel to eat it.\n\nAt this point I had lowered my rating from my original 4 to a three because my girlfriend's meal was a 2 at best and averaging the two scores gave me a 3 but soon that 3 would become it's final score of just 2!\n\nI asked for the check, the waitress brought over a pre-check with some charges on it, it said something about 2 towels, I asked what that was, it was the two wet naps that they had brought over for us to wash our hands with!\n\nSo please take my advise and avoid this place, the menu and restaurant look good but it's just not worth the aggravation.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 5, 2018",
